Third-party components and licenses
===================================

This file records licensing for third-party components under third_party/.
It is informational; each vendored source file or directory keeps its own
copyright and license notice.

MSFA (Dexed) -- vendored under third_party/msfa
-----------------------------------------------
- MSFA is the engine from Google's music-synthesizer-for-android project.
  The original files carry "Copyright 2012 Google Inc." and the Apache
  License 2.0.
- The copy used by Dexed includes later modifications (for example
  "Copyright 2016-2025 Pascal Gauthier") but keeps the Apache License 2.0
  headers. Dexed's README states that the msfa component stays Apache-2.0.
- Dexed's own plugin/application code and its patch/Cartridge code are
  GPL-3.0.
- The vendored copy keeps the upstream license headers. The Apache-2.0 text
  is in third_party/msfa/LICENSE, and the local changes/stubs are described in
  third_party/msfa/README.md.
- The preenFM3 firmware as a whole is distributed under GPL-3.0 (see
  ../LICENSE). Apache-2.0 code can be combined with GPL-3.0; the Apache-2.0
  files remain under Apache-2.0.

doctest -- vendored under third_party/doctest
--------------------------------------------
- doctest is a single-header C++ testing framework by Viktor Kirilov.
- The vendored copy is v2.4.11 and keeps its MIT license header; the full
  MIT text is in third_party/doctest/LICENSE.txt.
- It is used only by the host test target under tests/, not by the firmware.

9W9 / X0X -- vendored under third_party/9W9
-------------------------------------------
- 9W9 is a TR-909 emulation by athousanddetails (schwung-9W9). The vendored
  DSP is the bare-metal C port from X0X (charlesvestal/fm1-x0x),
  firmware/src/dsp/.
- The vendored files (drum909.c, drum909.h, drum909_dsp.h, fastmath.h,
  x0x_param.h) keep their GPL-3.0 SPDX headers. The preenFM3 firmware as a
  whole is GPL-3.0, so the licenses are compatible.
- assets/909/{hh,ride,crash}.wav and tools/gen_drum_samples.py also come from
  X0X; see assets/909/README.txt for the sample credits.

